WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.506
Hi! Books, doors and windows all have angles. Today we'll learn about angles and right angles, and compare their sizes.

2
00:00:10.656 --> 00:00:14.466
When two straight lines meet at a point, they make an angle.

3
00:00:14.616 --> 00:00:20.418
The corner of a book is a right angle. We mark a right angle with a small square.

4
00:00:20.568 --> 00:00:27.546
Some angles are smaller than a right angle, with a narrow opening. Some are bigger, with a wide opening.

5
00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:34.722
An angle's size depends only on how far the arms open, not on how long they are drawn.

6
00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:39.162
Fold a piece of paper twice to make a right angle tester.

7
00:00:39.312 --> 00:00:43.338
Rectangles and squares both have 4 right angles.

8
00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:48.570
A triangle has 3 angles. A pentagon has 5 angles.

9
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:54.642
At 3 o'clock, the hour hand and minute hand make a right angle.

10
00:00:54.792 --> 00:01:00.882
Watch out! Some pupils think longer arms make a bigger angle. That's wrong!

11
00:01:01.032 --> 00:01:07.026
If we draw the arms longer, the opening stays the same, so the angle stays the same size.

12
00:01:07.176 --> 00:01:12.282
To compare angles, look at how far the arms open.

13
00:01:12.432 --> 00:01:21.306
Your turn! How many right angles does a rectangle have? Pause and think.

14
00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:27.330
A rectangle has 4 right angles. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:36.066
Another one! How many angles does a triangle have? Pause and think.

16
00:01:36.216 --> 00:01:41.682
A triangle has 3 angles. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:41.832 --> 00:01:50.562
Here's another! What kind of angle is the corner of a book? Pause and think.

18
00:01:50.712 --> 00:01:56.394
The corner of a book is a right angle. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:56.544 --> 00:02:05.394
Try one more! What angle do the hands make at 3 o'clock? Pause and think.

20
00:02:05.544 --> 00:02:11.754
At 3 o'clock, the hands make a right angle. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:11.904 --> 00:02:24.858
Try one more! A door is opened very wide. Is the angle between the door and the wall bigger or smaller than a right angle? Pause and think.

22
00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:32.658
The opening is wider than a book's corner, so it's bigger than a right angle. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:32.808 --> 00:02:44.514
Last one! Scissors are opened just a little. Is that angle bigger or smaller than a right angle? Pause and think.

24
00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:51.426
The opening is narrow, so it's smaller than a right angle. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:51.576 --> 00:03:02.034
Remember: two straight lines that meet make an angle. A book's corner is a right angle. An angle's size depends on the opening, not the length of the arms.

26
00:03:02.184 --> 00:03:08.082
Today, make a paper right angle and look for right angles at home!

